/** @mainpage Abstract

    This documentation describes a library that encapsulates classic CAN frames
    into UDP datagrams and broadcasts them on a network interface.
    Symmetrically, it also provides functions to listen for those datagrams and
    extract their content.  The API it provides is independent of the target
    operating system.  It is described in detail in the book **"Real-Time
    Embedded Systems—Open-Source Operating Systems Perspective"**, by Ivan
    Cibrario Bertolotti and Gabriele Manduchi, 2nd Edition, CRC Press, Taylor &
    Francis Group, 2025.

    The library currently supports *Linux* and its in-kernel protocol stack,
    along with *FreeRTOS* on ESP32-based boards and the *lwIP* protocol stack.
    Its secondary goal is to show how to write portable code that works across
    very different operating environments.

*/
